#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114979 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/id #uuid "87bf279f-9f78-54cb-b9c3-e1bf1c5426ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-4505" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114980 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "359f4b72-60d2-54e2-b7ef-c48f1e3af708" :question/math-academy-id "e-4506" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5y=-3x \\\\ 6+x=-2+y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y=0 \\\\ x-y=-8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114981 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b87aa5eb-f689-5f34-baeb-f97c3f200552" :question/math-academy-id "e-4507" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x-15y=5 \\\\ 1x+0y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=1 \\\\ x=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcc7b819-d34d-5e43-95c9-c1b281f2d4c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285569} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc182d2-9706-5763-93dc-587dab323cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285570} {:answer/id #uuid "623abe45-ff87-5e43-9dc1-245c2962faf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+5y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285571} {:answer/id #uuid "baa1cfed-e269-547a-9c12-2e3d7b76faa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=-15 \\\\ 12x+6y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285572} {:answer/id #uuid "5674977b-88eb-5d70-9612-43da6db8de1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=15 \\\\ 4x+y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dc182d2-9706-5763-93dc-587dab323cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285570} :answer-field/id #uuid "d80dc95a-ccfe-5c63-add0-c28ed2aa747c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285568}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7dad4c0b-b40d-5232-bf24-f4b25c943bdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-130523" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & 25 \\\\ 12 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=15 \\\\ 12x+3y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285598 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3596704-6fa8-58b1-8392-a250a5444f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3596704-6fa8-58b1-8392-a250a5444f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285600} :answer-field/id #uuid "731a984d-b95d-5c89-a685-22b9784d90ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285599} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "feb45f9c-11e8-562c-94ca-719f9001fe66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feb45f9c-11e8-562c-94ca-719f9001fe66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285602} :answer-field/id #uuid "f415aea3-5475-5682-a17a-0b5011c5410b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285601} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b50707b5-4c9e-550d-a2ac-776967ac9fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b50707b5-4c9e-550d-a2ac-776967ac9fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285604} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1b4898b-0011-51e7-bc96-841a173d3dbc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f12c772c-b0c5-594f-8b5f-57f2dd4259cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f12c772c-b0c5-594f-8b5f-57f2dd4259cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285606} :answer-field/id #uuid "21b222cb-0f2d-588b-b05d-c5289a4f997b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bfa79505-f094-536b-8de1-28d863aaf777" :question/math-academy-id "q-317500" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-6y=4 \\\\ 3x+5y\\,=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $4$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. \nThe variable $x$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-6y=4 \\\\ 3x+5y\\,=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65eb3fcd-89b6-50d1-8030-8e0e856b8493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285609} {:answer/id #uuid "7eb2804d-566e-5894-9673-8e2e5f70f0d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65eb3fcd-89b6-50d1-8030-8e0e856b8493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285609} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b657339-550d-5381-ae3f-5e005e506ec4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285608} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c12c81-cbcd-5d39-ac3d-a523d98124ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98c12c81-cbcd-5d39-ac3d-a523d98124ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285612} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b9df299-3855-56ba-9143-e274a7d7fb31" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285611} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dd4d4fa-c097-55f2-9bb3-97cf9ef0b37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dd4d4fa-c097-55f2-9bb3-97cf9ef0b37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285614} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1c2edf-0660-5cef-90b2-8f6f60c0eb7f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cbf5118-38a1-5913-9c1f-50e22b2d244c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cbf5118-38a1-5913-9c1f-50e22b2d244c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285616} :answer-field/id #uuid "f19887aa-a43c-5431-8dde-6e40e1cb03ed" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af3e197c-8649-56f3-9c21-c51a5293b5c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-317506" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5x=10 \\\\ 4y=-12\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $10$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $10$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ Similarly, the variable $x$ does not appear in the second equation, which means that its coefficient is $0$ too. \n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5x+0y=10 \\\\ 0x+4y=-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9c343a1-d172-5942-8b4a-e0759aa92444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9c343a1-d172-5942-8b4a-e0759aa92444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285638} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e45197-bbc4-522c-9bbf-eabdba33f705" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e3d4d50-f411-58ef-9647-6592215b18f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e3d4d50-f411-58ef-9647-6592215b18f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285640} :answer-field/id #uuid "31d3dddc-5cdf-5458-b65d-64ce63b5e305" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25fce9dd-4418-571a-8006-fb53dba401f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25fce9dd-4418-571a-8006-fb53dba401f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285642} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4ee6fe0-01ce-5e92-9eb6-9df772c5c188" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285641} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bb1773c-6b74-5e2b-be8e-083c224ac9f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bb1773c-6b74-5e2b-be8e-083c224ac9f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285644} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c5af3c7-6c7b-5c54-9f0d-bf82d4af0887" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "837cc9d4-4e9c-5181-aa72-7d095c6ebf76" :question/math-academy-id "q-317530" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y-2x=9 \\\\ -5y\\,=-15,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-5$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $9$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $9$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=9 \\\\ 0x-5y=-15\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}]}
